<!-- ClickHouse's crash reports, turned off (workplan 0139, 2026-09-28).

     Privacy §8 names every party that receives anything, and the owner chose,
     for ops-telemetry: "Switch it off everywhere". ClickHouse was one of the
     parties nobody had named.

     The config.xml this image ships (programs/server/config.xml at
     v26.2.19.43-stable) sets

         <send_crash_reports>
             <enabled>true</enabled>
             <send_logical_errors>true</send_logical_errors>
             <endpoint>https://crash.clickhouse.com/</endpoint>

     so on a crash, and on a logical error, the server posts a report to
     ClickHouse, Inc. The code's own default is off: src/Daemon/CrashWriter.cpp
     reads send_crash_reports.enabled with `false`, and BaseDaemon.cpp reads
     send_logical_errors the same way. It is the shipped file that turns both
     on, so a file in config.d, merged over it, turns both off again.

     A file of its own rather than a line in clickhouse-override.xml, which is
     upstream's tuning verbatim and says so.

     `scripts/a-service-that-phones-home.unit.test.ts` reads this file through
     managed.yml's mount, and fails when either value is anything but false, or
     when a second mounted file also speaks of crash reports. -->
<clickhouse>
    <send_crash_reports>
        <enabled>false</enabled>
        <send_logical_errors>false</send_logical_errors>
    </send_crash_reports>
</clickhouse>
